/* probe-c6-mr-simp-e92-log-branch.mac — C6 e92 non-transition root cause.
   Maxima branch_5_50_base_84_g4204fb669, SBCL 2.6.7.
   Run: sh probes/maxima/probe-c6-mr-simp-e92-log-branch.run

   The 3.5 r10 replacement calls %mr_simp(u*diff(Px,x)/Px, x).  For the
   e92 family, u is a log-form antiderivative and the first ratsimp stage
   rewrites a log argument so that its numeric value changes (a Maxima
   log(-z) branch issue).  The probe measures the e92 nested integrand
   before/after %mr_simp at the driver's two numeric test points. */
ratprint: false$
f92: log(d*(a+c*x^2)^n)/(a*e+c*e*x^2)$
mm: _mr_pat_3_5_r10(f92, x)$
Px: geteqR(mm, '_mr_3_5_r10_Px)$
Qx: geteqR(mm, '_mr_3_5_r10_Qx)$
u: mr_int(1/Qx, x)$
